{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable","id":1283190,"title":"Are Strix playable?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-27T21:42:33-08:00","id":1283190,"title":"Are Strix playable?","content":"Are Strix playable considering that they're able to survive in sunlight unlike Kindred do or rather your closest 19th century literary vampire you can get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T22:20:39-08:00","id":1283199,"title":"","content":"Technically, the rules are there for you to do it. Practically, the rules are not designed to expect you to do this and don't make accommodations for it. Strix banes are stricter and less player-friendly than Kindred banes, incapacitating them more easily or complicating commonplace, everyday situations. They're stated not to earn beats or experiences, and even if you ignore this, they have no advancement rules for acquiring new trait dots with them, with Skill dots being stolen from hosts, Dread Power and Attribute growth tied to Shadow Potency, and Shadow Potency in turn solely increasing through centuries of age or diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T22:28:33-08:00","id":1283201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1283199#post1283199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, the rules are there for you to do it. Practically, the rules are not designed to expect you to do this and don't make accommodations for it. Strix banes are stricter and less player-friendly than Kindred banes, incapacitating them more easily or complicating commonplace, everyday situations. They're stated not to earn beats or experiences, and even if you ignore this, they have no advancement rules for acquiring new trait dots with them, with Skill dots being stolen from hosts, Dread Power and Attribute growth tied to Shadow Potency, and Shadow Potency in turn solely increasing through centuries of age or diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the answer is pretty much no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T00:21:47-08:00","id":1283216,"title":"","content":"Pretty much.<br /> <br /> While nothing is stopping you from forging ahead and making them playable, by RAW they were designed to be ST-only antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T09:26:58-08:00","id":1283285,"title":"","content":"That said, as long as everyone at the table agrees, that sounds like a fascinating Short Story. A Flock of Strix causing what mayhem they can and trying to out maneuver what would usually be the PCs but are this time ST chars. It sounds fascinating enough for a limited game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T10:07:30-08:00","id":1283297,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as written it's not impossible, but they're not built to accommodate the idea. That being said, I can imagine a scenario where you use basic vampire rules and just toss out Humanity, or replace it with something more alien. Make it more like Demon: The Fallen, where possessing an individual forces a strix to fall under certain limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T17:06:37-08:00","id":1283391,"title":"","content":"<b>Here's a fun idea!</b><br /> <br /> Play as Strix-possessed vampires, where you play as a vampire possessed by a Strix. Then, after one or two chapters of Strix shenanigans, the Striges leave their host bodies (your characters) and then you get to play 'Dude Where's My Car?' as your actual vampire characters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T19:05:25-08:00","id":1283617,"title":"","content":"Heres a question?!<br /> <br /> Can strix be bound?<br /> <br /> one of their most common powers defens from mind affecting Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> But binding them and sending them out sounds cool.<br /> <br /> As long as you <i>know </i>what your doing if you just think you know, your a goner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T19:15:39-08:00","id":1283621,"title":"","content":"One of the key elements of the strix is their chaos factor and wiliness, so having them bound by commands would eliminate a lot of their effectiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T20:43:34-08:00","id":1283637,"title":"","content":"as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar654_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"654\" data-vbnamecard=\"654\">xiongrey</a> said, a short story as the strix could be cool, like a create your own conflict (for when you go back to vampire)<br /> <br /> otherwise not practical to play as","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T04:15:09-08:00","id":1283681,"title":"","content":"Bind how? Generally speaking you can most certainly bind them as long as they don't have specific defences against your method of binding them. The difficulty (other than their commonly occurring immunity to mind affecting Disciplines) comes in you not knowing who to bind until it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T08:36:41-08:00","id":1283725,"title":"","content":"say with Cruac?<br /> <br /> Summoning and sending them off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T08:54:35-08:00","id":1283728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1283391#post1283391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Here's a fun idea!</b><br /> <br /> Play as Strix-possessed vampires, where you play as a vampire possessed by a Strix. Then, after one or two chapters of Strix shenanigans, the Striges leave their host bodies (your characters) and then you get to play 'Dude Where's My Car?' as your actual vampire characters!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As much as this sounds fun--especially the part where you spend an arc trying to figure out what the hell went wrong with your requiem, another more linear way to play it would be for a flock of stirges to engage in some synthesis with hapless mortals.<br /> <br /> They come out the other side as something much less than human and much more than pure Strix. Ditch Humanity for example, but keep the mechanics of vampire advancement and maybe let them play dread powers. The issue the Strix would have is that stupid human voice that keeps whining about doing &quot;mean things&quot; like flaying people alive to get at the juicy bits, and asking them to play nice with people who seem to think they should know the host....<br /> <br /> (Edit: you could look at this as a &quot;reverse Beast&quot;, even.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS Edit: <b><i>why </i></b>a flock of stirges would want to do this is something that the group could attempt to answer themselves, especially as the process of synthesis is... jarring to strix memories and motivations. It's basically a &quot;here hold my beer&quot; moment for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 01-31-2019, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T08:58:35-08:00","id":1283729,"title":"","content":"If you have a ritual for it, sure. But I would be extremely suspicious about such rituals in case they're invented by Strix to lure the ritualist into a false sense of security. It might actually only summon Strix without binding them, or the binding is more literal than expected and the Strix is actually only bound to be in proximity to the ritualist rather than bound to follow the ritualist's orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T13:14:02-08:00","id":1283782,"title":"","content":"I could see some inventive bastard coming up with the idea of diablorizing a strix, and possibly inviting his coterie into the ritualistic act. I mean--it's ok, right, because the strix isn't a Kindred and rules don't apply, right?<br /> <br /> Nothing could possibly go wrong I'm sure, and you totally wouldn't get some weird shadow-and-ash malevolence replacing what was, with new perspective, your mundane and somewhat tepid, beast....<br /> <br /> No sirree.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T14:59:12-08:00","id":1283804,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say a Strix becomes playable when it fuses with a human body and results in a vampire. Before that you could sort of play one, but the rules aren\u2019t really amenable, and, more importantly, they\u2019re completely inhuman, so a lot of the point of the game is lost. Not unlike playing a Draugr (which is arguably an embodied Strix).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T06:27:46-08:00","id":1283906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1283804#post1283804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say a Strix becomes playable when it fuses with a human body and results in a vampire. Before that you could sort of play one, but the rules aren\u2019t really amenable, and, more importantly, they\u2019re completely inhuman, so a lot of the point of the game is lost. Not unlike playing a Draugr (which is arguably an embodied Strix).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly unless your embodied strix has the flaw of gluttony or wrath (and, even then), they're more collected and reasonable than Draugr are. Those are people totally lost to the Beast and only able to reason with basic hunting instincts. They do not have access [conscious choice in use of] to the more mental Disciplines and are motivated by the basic desires of food and safety. The low cunning some show is not the sort of malevolence the strix are known to engage in.<br /> <br /> That said, strix vary a great deal, and some are closer to Draugr for sure.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> Edit: Fair enough <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>. On reflection I seem to recall a Draugr could use something like Dominate in order to pin down prey long enough to close and seal the attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":".  Because eating crow lets you turn into one, later. 01-31-2019, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T06:46:25-08:00","id":1283911,"title":"","content":"Small nitpick: Draugr still have access to all their (non-Blood Sorcery) Disciplines. They are just highly unlikely to ever use them.<br /> But yeah, Strix supposedly being the disembodied Beasts of Kindred is just something they say to rile Kindred up. It's possible there exists some kind of feral Strix that are also reduced to base instincts just like a draugr, but those would be an exception. The average Strix is more than capable of higher reasoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T12:23:27-08:00","id":1283981,"title":"","content":"One of the defining characteristics of the Strix is that they're alien and inscrutable. Playing them, while possible, would dispel a lot of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T13:14:31-08:00","id":1283993,"title":"","content":"I might allow it for a one shot. The catch is that you get no beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T15:11:17-08:00","id":1284015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1283993#post1283993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might allow it for a one shot. The catch is that you get no beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it\u2019s a one shot, experience gains are irrelevant anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T15:19:10-08:00","id":1284019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1283981#post1283981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the defining characteristics of the Strix is that they're alien and inscrutable. Playing them, while possible, would dispel a lot of that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly doesn't seem like it would be much different from Unchained Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T16:39:10-08:00","id":1284032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1284019#post1284019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly doesn't seem like it would be much different from Unchained Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unchained have to play into humanity for survival and were already designed to interface with humanity to begin with at a minimum, and often Fall and subsequently motivated by human connections and experiences. They're human enough that the ways they differ is basically within range enough that a human roleplaying as one is close enough that all you need to do to properly get it is flip the perspective on why the minor oddnesses of inhumanity are there.<br /> <br /> The Strix don't have any of that and as such lean heavily into their alien instincts and spiral outwards at odd angles for that. Without something to root them in humanity, their cruelty, malice, and ambitions are allowed to just get <i>weird</i>, and that's before accounting that they universally have <i>something</i> (of one sort or another) against humanity. That's a far cry from the PC Demon experience, which is fair-they are completely different games, as demons have to hide and interact with humanity to get things done while the Strix are Gleeful Abandon and Inhumanity incarnate, with a bare minimum requirement to hide and otherwise a whole lot of freedom to fuck around with anyone however they want.<br /> <br /> Being blunt, asides from dispelling that alien malice, it's also just an obnoxious mindset to have on the players side of things. Characters that behave like the Strix invariably interrupt and often frustrate the player group-they're kind of troll characters on the PC side. They work as antagonists because of the way they are controlled and ideally used as sparingly as the story needs, but as protagonists, the character type just sucks for anything resembling a cohesive gaming experience.<br /> <br /> So....no, this doesn't hold water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T16:41:41-08:00","id":1284033,"title":"","content":"Unrelated, the answer to &quot;How do I portray Bram Stoker's version of Dracula in Requiem <i>exactly?</i>&quot; is &quot;By doing it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Literally, just do it. grab what you need, slap it together, and then just do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T03:10:13-08:00","id":1284095,"title":"","content":"You could just let vampires go out in the sun, but keep the daysleep rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T07:41:25-08:00","id":1284132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1284032#post1284032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So....no, this doesn't hold water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I feel like you could do something kind of interesting in a one-on-one and a lot of time-jumps. Some of the suggested origins are &quot;cracks in the deep dark places of the world, coalescing out of the blood of <b>massed graves</b>, final breath of <b>murder victims</b>, <b>funeral pyre smoke</b> of murderers.&quot; (bolded options are where I think are RPable when combined with vindictiveness).<br /> <br /> Example: I have a Strix that in my current game that I've got associated with babies (a lot of old vampire stories seem to just be about SIDs). So my headcannon is that a long time ago a plague hit some Indonesian village and wiped out the youngest generation. <br /> <br /> So take a bunch of people with no coping skills or ability to understand what is happening and have them die painfully. Then take the negative emotions -- anger and outrage and loss and want -- and distill it into a single insubstantial demon owl. All you can do is watch and feed and scream. You're brand new, and don't have any memories. You feel drawn to people and places of warmth and care. You don't know why, but seeing loving parents drives you into a jealous rage. Nobody wants you. If you run into other Strix, they try to eat you. As time passes, you don't really hold on to memories so much as... emotional sediment.<br /> <br /> I think it's got the makings of a a good story. Each scene is at least a few years apart. Do a handful of sessions, each skips forward about a century. Play it from bereft baby Strixling to evil mastermind with no memory of its origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T16:43:52-08:00","id":1284239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1283981#post1283981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the defining characteristics of the Strix is that they're alien and inscrutable. Playing them, while possible, would dispel a lot of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another defining characteristic is that each one is unique therefore understanding one is not an understanding of any other Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T02:27:28-08:00","id":1284309,"title":"","content":"No, the Strix are not designed to be playable. It would also be counter to the setting material for them to be so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T04:47:31-08:00","id":1284318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1284309#post1284309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Strix are not designed to be playable. It would also be counter to the setting material for them to be so.</div> </div> </div> </div>it would require major Rule c hanges<br /> <br /> Someones probably coming up with a storytellers vault supplement as we speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> A strix bound by some kind of sorcery, or unique discipline would be fun to see in action to 'remote embrace'<br /> <br /> or posses a revenant in a enemy city to s tart organizing a Coup against the current Regime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T12:03:03-08:00","id":1284378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1283190-are-strix-playable?p=1284318#post1284318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it would require major Rule c hanges<br /> <br /> Someones probably coming up with a storytellers vault supplement as we speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> A strix bound by some kind of sorcery, or unique discipline would be fun to see in action to 'remote embrace'<br /> <br /> or posses a revenant in a enemy city to s tart organizing a Coup against the current Regime.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Prince needs to be kidnapped, are you a bad enough Strix to do the deed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T11:07:26-08:00","id":1285608,"title":"","content":"No. They're not playable and you shouldn't play them, shame on your for wanting to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}